---
description: |
  Updates the SOC Prime Active Threat catalog from OSINT Inventory Info.

  The catalog is a lookup table keyed by Sigma rule ID, the ID that detection
  findings carry in `finding_info.analytic.uid`. Each entry holds the list of
  OCSF `osint` objects of all Active Threats that the rule belongs to, as
  `socprime::catalog` computes it.

  The operator expects the output of `socprime::ocsf::map` for the complete
  set of threats, because it replaces the entry of every rule it sees.

  Declare the lookup table in your configuration:

  ```yaml
  # contexts/socprime-active-threats.yaml
  type: lookup-table
  ```
args:
  named:
    - name: context_name
      type: string
      default: socprime-active-threats
      description: Lookup-table context to update.
---

socprime::catalog
context_update $context_name, key=uid, value=threats
